---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { network, forms } from '../lib/network';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---

<Base title="Join" description="How a lab joins the network and how the review works.">
  <h1>Join</h1>
  <p class="lead">Membership is by lab. A PI submits one form; a coordinator reviews it; the lab appears on the roster.</p>

  <div class="actions" style="margin-top:0">
    <a class="btn primary" href={forms.lab}>Submit a lab</a>
    <a class="btn" href={url('calendar.ics')}>Follow the seminars</a>
  </div>

  <h2>Who</h2>
  <dl class="facts">
    <dt>Member lab</dt>
    <dd>A PI-led group at an institution in the Greater Bay Area. Listed, hosts seminars in turn, invites speakers on behalf of all.</dd>
    <dt>Affiliate lab</dt>
    <dd>A lab elsewhere that takes part regularly. Listed with a badge.</dd>
    <dt>Everyone else</dt>
    <dd>
      Students, postdocs, anyone: subscribe to the <a href={url('calendar.ics')}>calendar</a>. For the announcement list,
      which carries meeting links,{' '}
      {network.contact_email ? (
        <a href={`mailto:${network.contact_email}`}>email us</a>
      ) : (
        <>ask any member PI or <a href={forms.issues}>open an issue</a></>
      )}.
    </dd>
  </dl>

  <h2>How</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li>Open the <a href={forms.lab}>lab form</a>. It needs a free GitHub account; a colleague can submit for you.</li>
    <li>Name, institution, city, up to eight keywords, two sentences on the lab. A photo is optional.</li>
    <li>Tick the consent box. Name, photo and affiliation are published under CC BY 4.0.</li>
    <li>A pull request is opened for you. A coordinator merges it, usually within days, and the lab is live.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Also</h2>
  <dl class="facts">
    <dt><a href={forms.nomination}>Nominate a speaker</a></dt>
    <dd>Anyone may. Nominations go to the coordinators and are not published on the site.</dd>
    <dt><a href={forms.event}>Propose an event</a></dt>
    <dd>Seminars, workshops, summer schools. See the <a href={url('docs/speaker-kit/')}>speaker kit</a> for the format.</dd>
    <dt><a href={forms.tutorial}>Share a tutorial</a></dt>
    <dd>Notebooks, courses, recordings. The material stays where you host it.</dd>
    <dt><a href={forms.position}>Post a position</a></dt>
    <dd>PhD, postdoc, RA, faculty. Listings expire on their deadline.</dd>
  </dl>

  <p class="small muted" style="margin-top:2.5rem">
    To change or remove an entry, edit its file by pull request or open an issue. The rules are in the{' '}
    <a href={url('docs/charter/')}>charter</a> and the <a href={url('docs/privacy-and-consent/')}>privacy statement</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
